{"Title":"An Act relative to implementing a blue alert system in the Commonwealth","BillNumber":"S1591","DocketNumber":"SD585","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T12:22:21.88"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T12:22:21.88"},{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-10-30T17:22:01.2933333"},{"Id":"RCF0","Name":"Ryan C. Fattman","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RCF0","ResponseDate":"2024-05-01T10:48:02.8933333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1591/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Tarr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1591) of Bruce E. Tarr for legislation relative to implementing a blue alert system in the Commonwealth.  Public Safety and Homeland Security.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 18¾ of chapter 6A of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2008 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following clause:-\r\n\t(10) to develop and implement a statewide blue alert system to be activated when law enforcement officials are searching for an individual who is wanted in the serious injury or killing of a police officer, state trooper, or other law enforcement official.  \r\n\tSECTION 2. Chapter 6A of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2008 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after section 19A the following section:-\r\n\tSection 19B. The executive office of public safety shall coordinate the implementation of a statewide blue alert system, pursuant to section 21 of chapter 22.  \r\n\tSECTION 3. Chapter 22 of The General Laws are hereby amended by adding the following section:- \r\n\tSection 21.\r\n\tTHE STATEWIDE BLUE ALERT SYSTEM\r\n\tSection 1. The following terms as used in this chapter shall, unless the context clearly appears otherwise, have the following meanings:\r\n\t“Executive office”, the executive office of public safety.\r\n\t\"Law enforcement agency\", a  law enforcement agency with jurisdiction over the investigation of a crime resulting in the serious injury or death of a police officer, state trooper, or other law enforcement official.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}